{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/1/a619f19f5c098bd1b3c4d6d701969524f6c19bab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e9a8498a77bde1bb0734f91c4e6f1011888ae7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{x^{x+1}}{x+1}  \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = x^{x}\\ln x  \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = x^{x}  \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = \\dfrac{x^{x}}{\\ln x}  \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = x^{x} + x^{x}\\ln x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"718\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46321a9073b6d725f7637ed31bfc826becd2382a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. We take the natural log and use the logarithm property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a487f6cd1f5ca58fa5937ea0186cc0ddcc8dc46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{b}a^{c} = c\\log_{b}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/b/73ba29f7574c79bdf48471ab72b14057cadde233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ln y = x \\ln x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. Performing implicit differentiation, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\t\\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ \\ln y \\right] &amp;= \\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ x\\ln x \\right]\\\\\n\t\\frac{dy}{dx} \\cdot \\frac{1}{y} &amp;=  x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + 1 \\cdot \\ln x\\\\\n\t\\frac{dy}{dx} &amp;= y(1 + \\ln x)\n\\end{align*}\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/46321a9073b6d725f7637ed31bfc826becd2382a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x^{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/061c04998a3fd32e11102d20bc7f5d2e9b5acc41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dx} = x^{x} + x^{x}\\ln x }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"185\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Con